e.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T00:10:18-08:00","id":1346089,"title":"","content":"My favorites so far are Assassin's Creed: Black Flag, and Red Dead Redemption. Besides that, the Total War series (Shogun II is my favorite), Age of Empires on Apknite is worth playing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25763-polaroid","name":"polaroid","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T02:50:23-08:00","id":1346109,"title":"","content":"My friend played Red Dead Redemption. He loved it. But I mostly meant tabletop RPGs like World of Darkness and Trinity Continuum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T05:29:29-08:00","id":1346133,"title":"","content":"Penelope, that's an ad bot","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T07:14:50-08:00","id":1346149,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7920_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7920\" data-vbnamecard=\"7920\">Master Aquatosic</a> thanks. Now I feel like an idiot lol. I'm usually good at spotting those. Just didn't expect to see one here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T19:04:42-08:00","id":1352093,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s awesome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><a href=\"https://theimpossible-quiz.co/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">the impossible quiz</span></a><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"> free</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25820-milesgooding","name":"milesgooding","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T00:38:08-08:00","id":1352116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343573-is-your-gaming-group-interested-in-the-theoretical-historical-aspects-of-gaming#post1343573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stuff like the themes of Princess: the Hopeful or how old the Second City is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually to some degree yes, but on two occasions they've gone... Overboard maybe?<br /> <br /> I had my entire chronicle plans utterly derailed because my players got hooked on my non-canon version of France in VtM. To be fair, there was a long-thought-deceased bloodline (rumored to be a 14th clan purged from historical records) directly ripped off from Holy Blood Holy Grail, an appearance by Boudica (a Nosferatu), secret vaults in cemetaries filled with traps, and so much more. Most of which hadn't been initially planned (more reacting to sudden and unexpected events), nor did it have <b>anything at all</b> to do with the original story I was weaving about a possible infernalist among the Primogen. It was fun, though looking back on some of the ideas I had at the time, I question my judgement in implementing them.<br /> <br /> In the other case, with mostly the same players, I used a whole-cloth created city in California, complete with a history filled with tidbits in case the players started looking for them. This one didn't go quite as off-the-rails because I kind of anticipated the players going this direction. And the reveals were never as dramatic, but still pretty memorable.<br /> <br /> Mostly, when my players get into the setting history, it's musings and discussing. But occasionally it <i>does </i>devolve into a trope-filled Indiana Jones-inspired B-movie plot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T04:14:30-08:00","id":1352136,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar700_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"700\" data-vbnamecard=\"700\">Vysha</a> I read Holy Blood Holy Grail. Some of the stuff in there about the Freemasons was really interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}